1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,800
<i>Celestial Insurance's annual</i>
<i>premium revenue is nearly 100 billion.</i>

3
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:48,040
Even if you come up with a dozen or two

4
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:51,200
of these pet insurance scenarios,

5
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:54,040
they can only generate
at most several billion in premiums.

6
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,480
What impact could that possibly have

7
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:58,040
on Celestial Insurance's
multi-billion-yuan business?

8
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:01,640
I haven't collected enough materials.

9
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,560
In that case,

10
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:06,560
why did you tell Ma Ke
you were confident in your proposal?

11
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:18,040
The Celestial Insurance project
has been dragging on for too long.

12
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,280
Since the client wasn't happy
with the first version,

13
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,760
we can't just phone it in

14
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:24,320
for the second proposal
after all the time we've put in.

15
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,000
These slides are all descriptive.

16
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:32,040
No hard data to back them up.

17
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:35,760
And there's no holistic view
from the client's perspective!

18
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:38,840
This isn't Maxmise's standard.

19
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
- I'd like to explain.
- Sorry.

20
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,280
I don't want to waste everyone's time.

21
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:48,640
Ma Ke, as the project manager,
what's your take?

22
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,600
Alright.

23
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,440
NEXT STEPS

24
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:06,520
Mr. Pi.

25
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,320
My approach starts
with the key value drivers

26
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,640
of their current business.

27
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:12,480
I built a value tree
for Celestial Insurance.

28
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:23,880
I re-identified the key value drivers
of their current business.

29
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:29,200
The focus is on using AI
to optimize existing business processes.

30
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:50,080
<i>This proposal is far too complicated.</i>

31
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:53,160
<i>I'd suggest redoing it with a focus</i>

32
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:55,640
<i>on scenario-based big data business</i>
<i>and enhancing the customer experience.</i>

33
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,640
Mr. Pi, this is my proposal.

34
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,280
Ma Ke did a great job.

35
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,760
Everyone, good work.

36
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,480
<i>Mr. Pi once told me a story.</i>

37
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,440
There was a herder out on the grassland,

38
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:27,080
tending his sheep.

39
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:29,360
Suddenly, a man showed up.

40
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:31,880
He was wearing a shirt and tie,
carrying a briefcase.

41
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,360
He said to the herder,

42
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:36,680
"Hey, sir. I can give you
a high-end service.

43
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:40,880
I just counted your sheep. You have 548."

44
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:44,000
The herder said, "Yeah. How did you know?"

45
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:47,320
The man said, "I just tapped
into the satellite matrix up there.

46
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:48,720
That's how I counted.

47
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:52,120
So I'm taking this sheep
as my service fee."

48
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:54,760
Then the herder said, "Wait a minute.

49
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:57,480
Are you a consultant?"

50
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,600
The man was puzzled.
He went, "How did you know?"

51
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:03,000
"First, you showed up uninvited.

52
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:07,480
Second, you told me data I already knew.

53
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:09,760
Third, that's not a sheep you're holding.

54
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:11,200
It's my dog."

55
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:16,000
This is how ordinary people
misunderstand us, consultants.

56
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:19,120
They think we're
just smooth talkers. Right?

57
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:22,520
I'm sharing this story so you remember it

58
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:24,640
as a cautionary tale.

59
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:29,040
Don't let yourself
become the main character in this story.

60
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:35,920
Hot chocolate.

61
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:41,280
Thanks.

62
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:45,280
This kind of thing happens.
I've been through it too.

63
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:47,680
You have too?

64
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:49,840
That's just how Ma Ke is.

65
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:52,000
He used to be pretty good at his job,

66
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:54,040
but over the last couple of years,
with more going on at home,

67
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,640
his focus hasn't been on work.

68
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:57,680
He often takes credit for our work.

69
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,640
But he's good at networking.

70
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:03,200
Most of Celestial Insurance's projects
came from him drinking with clients.

71
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,360
That's why he's still at this company.

72
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:09,360
The project progress has been poor lately.

73
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:11,520
He probably figured
Mr. Pi would be back early,

74
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:13,600
so he took your proposal
and passed it off as his own.

75
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:15,240
And none of you ever pushed back?

76
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:17,520
Some people did object to his ways before,

77
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:19,000
but they got pushed out pretty quickly.

78
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,560
I've been with Ma Ke
since I joined the company.

79
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:22,760
I know him too well.

80
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,600
He's not a good person,

81
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:26,600
but the bonuses he gives out are generous.

82
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:29,600
Among the new hires,
he wouldn't dare touch Bu Tianna,

83
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,880
so he targeted you.

84
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:34,480
He set a trap to humiliate you in public.

85
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,520
Then, while you're still processing it,

86
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:38,640
he takes your proposal
to Mr. Pi and gets the credit.

87
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:43,080
After a maneuver like that,
most people just have to swallow it.

88
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:46,520
But I don't want to be
one of the silent majority.

89
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:49,720
Sorry, I didn't warn you sooner.

90
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:53,200
But you know the saying,
"If you don't bend, you break."

91
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,160
Lin Long is already on leave.

92
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:58,080
What happens if you go to war
with your direct supervisor?

93
00:06:58,160 --> 00:06:59,480
Who do you think the company
will side with?

94
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:02,120
Knowing Ma Ke,

95
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:04,080
he probably left no evidence
for you to hold onto.

96
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,360
Right.

97
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:09,280
That night, everyone else had gone home,

98
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:10,560
so there were no witnesses,

99
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:12,520
and he just borrowed my ideas.

100
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,200
He never asked
for the original slide files,

101
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:16,000
so there's no physical evidence either.

102
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:18,600
Even if I made a scene,
he'd just say it was

103
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:21,480
a similar line of thinking that came
out of our team discussions. Right?

104
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,480
So I just have to accept it.

105
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:28,920
So we can't lose this job
over a moment of anger.

106
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:32,960
Don't be upset.

107
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,480
The world is just that harsh.

108
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,040
Is it?

109
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,960
Such simple slides.

110
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,920
Not like your usual style.

111
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,680
Just a stumble.

112
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,320
The final team review
isn't due yet anyway.

113
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:16,720
I'll redo the proposal with a new angle.

114
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:17,880
I might still beat you.

115
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:22,520
I'm going to talk to the CEO's office now
to reschedule the interviews.

116
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,880
Did Ma Ke do something?

117
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:27,880
Is that why you got so worked up
at the weekly meeting?

118
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:33,440
No. I just wasn't good enough.

119
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:34,559
I'm off.

120
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:37,480
Then try to outdo me!

121
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:42,120
Hello, Ms. Yu. I'm Xu Chi from Maxmise.

122
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,039
Have a seat.

123
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:45,560
Thank you so much for coming today.

124
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:48,280
Of all the people Ma Ke has wronged,

125
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:50,480
she's recovered the fastest.

126
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:53,320
She's someone
who can achieve great things.

127
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,760
You bet.

128
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:04,560
Didn't we already send you the reports?

129
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:06,800
Yes. We've read the reports.

130
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,680
But they don't go deep enough.

131
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:11,280
So we wanted to dig
into the real pain points

132
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:13,480
of frontline business leaders
like you, Ms. Yu.

133
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:18,240
The real pain point is you guys
constantly bothering us.

134
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,960
Business folks are busy.

135
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:23,280
One call from headquarters,
and they pull us in from the branches.

136
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:26,440
All kinds of interviews,
meetings, and training.

137
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:29,280
Come on, we all have sales targets to hit.

138
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,400
We don't have time to sit around
chatting with you.

139
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
How about this? Let me speed things up.

140
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,880
I'll only take half an hour
of your time, alright?

141
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:42,040
- Ten minutes.
- Okay.

142
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,960
From a practical business perspective,

143
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:48,560
which scenarios or functions
does your department

144
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:50,720
need digital transformation in the most?

145
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,680
How would I know?

146
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:55,320
Our branch staff doesn't have
that high an education level.

147
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:57,800
They wouldn't understand
all that digital stuff.

148
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,320
You don't have to be that specific.

149
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:02,320
Just give me a general sense.

150
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,800
Your nose is bleeding.

151
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,280
- Take it.
- Thanks.

152
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:12,680
Don't tilt your head up. Keep it down.

153
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:15,200
Give me your hand.

154
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:16,520
- Here.
- No, it's fine.

155
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,560
Don't worry.

156
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:20,280
I used to get nosebleeds all the time too.
I'd just pinch right here.

157
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,880
The bleeding would stop in a bit.

158
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,560
Did I pinch too hard?

159
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:31,480
Bear with it.

160
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:36,840
Have… Have you been wronged?

161
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:40,160
Is it work or your boyfriend?

162
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:44,600
I've been there.

163
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:46,680
This is not just due
to getting overheated.

164
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:49,760
This is you being pushed around
and holding it all inside.

165
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:52,440
But you just have to take it.

166
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:55,160
Once the tears and blood are out,

167
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:56,200
the anger settles.

168
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:59,600
There'll always be a chance
to get even later.

169
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,040
Thanks.

170
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:02,680
Don't mention it.

171
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:05,160
Let's see. Did it stop?

172
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,200
Young lady…

173
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:16,680
I'm so sorry. I… I took up
so much of your time.

174
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:18,280
Let's continue.

175
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:20,720
Xu.

176
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:24,800
Take my advice.
You're not happy in this job anyway,

177
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:27,680
and I really need
to get back to the branch.

178
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:29,920
Let's not waste any more time. Alright?

179
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:31,600
How about this?

180
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:33,800
Just ride with me back to the branch.

181
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:35,160
We can talk on the way.

182
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,320
Sort out our thoughts properly.

183
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:39,560
It's better than flailing around
like headless chickens right now.

184
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:42,480
- I…
- Let's go.

185
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:58,840
- Thanks.
- No problem.

186
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:03,760
Xu.

187
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,520
After talking with you the whole way,

188
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:08,640
I can tell you're not the type
to put on airs.

189
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,320
Let me give you a heads-up.

190
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:13,240
No matter how many times you redo it,

191
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:15,720
Maxmise's proposal won't get approved.

192
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:17,880
So don't waste too much effort on it.

193
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:19,120
Why?

194
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,640
NO. 92, YONG'AN ROAD

195
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:56,360
XU CHI LOVES MOM

196
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:05,080
Mom.

197
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:10,440
I got bullied at work today.

198
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:14,720
These slides are all descriptive.

199
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:16,760
No hard data to back them up.

200
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,840
- I'd like to explain.
- Sorry.

201
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:20,960
I don't want to waste everyone's time.

202
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:24,680
I even cried in front of other people.

203
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:25,960
So embarrassing.

204
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:29,720
This is you being pushed around
and holding it all inside.

205
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:33,960
Once the tears and blood are out,
the anger settles.

206
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:37,640
There'll always be a chance
to get even later.

207
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:43,760
Mom, go beat him up for me. Alright?

208
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:50,080
Xu. Don't be too upset.

209
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:56,560
My colleagues all know
how attached you are to this place.

210
00:13:56,640 --> 00:14:00,080
But sometimes these things
just come down to timing.

211
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:04,640
Huang didn't tell you?

212
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:06,200
The owner of Unit 201 was willing to sell.

213
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,640
It was sold last Tuesday.

214
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,240
Sold?

215
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:11,800
‪Yes.

216
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:16,040
Unit 201 was sold?

217
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,400
Huang never told me.

218
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:18,360
Where is he?

219
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,520
He took his commission and quit.
Went back to his hometown.

220
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:22,560
Our industry has high turnover.

221
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:28,280
Xu… Are you okay? You…

222
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:29,880
Please don't scare me like that.

223
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:35,480
NO. 92, YONG'AN ROAD

224
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:43,640
Have some water.

225
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,520
Was it really sold?

226
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:52,120
This is the place I've been waiting for.

227
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,640
It's my mom's old apartment.

228
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:56,640
I didn't even get a chance
to see it inside,

229
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,640
and it's gone.

230
00:14:58,280 --> 00:14:59,680
The contract has been signed online.

231
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:00,920
Please don't be too upset.

232
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:03,080
I've been thinking about it for you.

233
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:05,560
Once his kid gets into school,
he'll probably sell.

234
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:07,640
We're the only agency at this entrance.

235
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:09,480
He'll have to list with us
when the time comes.

236
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:11,160
I'll keep an eye out for you.

237
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,920
The market is still trending down anyway.

238
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,160
Once you have the funds ready,

239
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:19,800
I can offer a little above market
and get Unit 201 back for you.

240
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:21,960
- Really?
- Really.

241
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:23,880
Then I'm counting on you.

242
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:26,280
As soon as I have the money,
I'm buying it.

243
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,560
I'll get you a nice big bonus
when it's done.

244
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:28,880
Xu, actually,

245
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:31,840
- there are similar units upstairs--
- I don't want those. I only want this one.

246
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:34,600
Alright. Let me add you on WeChat.

247
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:36,600
Let me know if anything comes up, okay?

248
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,600
- Wait--
- Scan my QR code.

249
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:40,240
Please, just do me a favor.

250
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:42,280
Just come look at a few places with me.

251
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:43,440
It's almost the end of the month.

252
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:45,080
If I don't hit my showing quota,

253
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:47,200
I'll lose my performance bonus.

254
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:53,400
Xu, you're so kind.

255
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:55,520
I'll make sure
to keep an eye on Unit 201 for you.

256
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:59,160
Our line of work isn't easy.

257
00:15:59,240 --> 00:16:01,920
Door-knocking, showings,
and meetings every day.

258
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,240
I thought it'd be easier
than selling insurance.

259
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,560
You used to sell insurance?

260
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:09,360
Yeah. I was a top agent.

261
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:10,760
Deputy director of the sales branch.

262
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:12,720
I even qualified
for the Million Dollar Round Table.

263
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:13,760
BLESSING

264
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:14,840
You're pulling my leg.

265
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:19,400
A branch director
makes at least 200,000 a year.

266
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:20,840
Why switch to real estate?

267
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:26,480
Look. This is me at the awards ceremony.

268
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:27,880
I just had bad luck.

269
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:31,240
I set up a slush fund in my department
and got caught. They fired me.

270
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:34,840
You're from Celestial?

271
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:38,800
We went to their company,
but they wouldn't agree,

272
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:40,360
and they wouldn't say why.

273
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:43,160
We went to Ms. Yu,
and she wouldn't agree either.

274
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:45,600
Xu, you came to the right person.

275
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:48,000
You know why Ms. Yu says
no proposal will ever get approved?

276
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:50,480
Because the business side
at Celestial will never agree!

277
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:51,400
Why?

278
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:55,160
Seventy percent of Celestial's employees
are salespeople out in the field.

279
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:58,000
Combining letters and reports
has already cut everyone's commissions.

280
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,800
If they go digital,
they'll have to share data for free.

281
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:01,440
That's basically giving away
all their hard-earned

282
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,120
business resources to others.

283
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,720
And once it's digitalized,

284
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:06,599
it'll probably all go
to the Internet Business Division.

285
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:08,079
They have separate accounting.

286
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:10,359
That's essentially taking money
from other divisions.

287
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:13,000
For that reason alone,
Ms. Yu and her people won't like you.

288
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:20,480
So at Celestial, aside from
the executives close to the CEO,

289
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:23,920
most employees actually don't want
digital transformation?

290
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:27,599
At least when I was there,
that's how everyone felt.

291
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:29,840
Their boss hired you, consultants.

292
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,760
No one dares to object openly,

293
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:34,080
so they find ways during review meetings.

294
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:36,400
Version one doesn't sit well
with one set of branches,

295
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:38,600
and version two
gets shot down by the rest.

296
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:40,800
I get it.

297
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:45,480
Maybe I can take back what's mine soon.

298
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,680
<i>You sure you want to work</i>
<i>alongside the salespeople?</i>

299
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:52,880
I'm sure.

300
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,720
Whatever they do, I do.

301
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:58,800
From field agent sales
to internal claims and underwriting,

302
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,880
I'll spend at least three days
in each department.

303
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:02,200
That's the only way I can figure out

304
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:04,040
the business pain points
you can't put into words.

305
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:07,120
You sure talk big.

306
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:08,680
But these are tough jobs.

307
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:10,720
Don't come crying when you get burnt out.

308
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:14,280
Still, tears from pushing myself

309
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,840
are better than those
from being pushed around.

310
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:18,480
I'll get some veterans
to show you the ropes.

311
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,960
HOME INSURANCE
PROTECTING EVERY CORNER OF YOUR HOME

312
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,640
- Let's bike.
- Okay.

313
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:33,280
<i>Go MIA again?</i>

314
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,640
<i>Sorry. I've been buried</i>
<i>in the project all week,</i>

315
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:40,000
<i>working around the clock.</i>

316
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:41,240
<i>My phone died.</i>

317
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:43,640
<i>You're busier than me now.</i>

318
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:44,840
<i>How's the project going?</i>

319
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:47,360
<i>Did you have your internal proposal</i>
<i>review meeting yet?</i>

320
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:48,360
‪YE XINZHI, XU CHI

321
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:50,160
<i>It went pretty well.</i>

322
00:19:50,240 --> 00:19:51,680
<i>What did you need?</i>

323
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:57,120
- <i>Are you off work?</i>
- <i>Yes.</i>

324
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:09,840
- Hello?
- Hello.

325
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:16,160
The project's on track,
so I didn't mention it.

326
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:18,120
I'm really fine.

327
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:21,240
I'm at the hotel right now,

328
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:23,320
munching on chips and drinking cola.

329
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:25,440
I've been to your place before.

330
00:20:25,520 --> 00:20:26,680
Not a single snack in sight.

331
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,920
<i>And you don't usually snack anyway.</i>

332
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:29,920
<i>Are you lying to me?</i>

333
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,760
I really am at a hotel. I'm really fine.

334
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:38,200
Given your track record
of running off in the middle of the night,

335
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:39,280
your credibility is low.

336
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:41,360
Switch to video.

337
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:43,960
No, no.

338
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:45,920
My room is a mess.

339
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:46,880
<i>Xu Chi.</i>

340
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:50,000
Where are you really?
Why are you being so evasive?

341
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:55,280
Give me a minute.

342
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:16,280
See? I'm at a hotel, right?

343
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:17,840
<i>I see it.</i>

344
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:19,640
<i>I'm not lying to you.</i>

345
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:21,840
<i>Why don't you believe me?</i>

346
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:25,080
Sorry. I was just a little worried
about you.

347
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:28,000
<i>Something about the way</i>
<i>you were talking felt off.</i>

348
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,600
Is there a problem with the project?

349
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:34,440
I didn't want to tell you
because if I did,

350
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:36,560
you'd definitely try to help me
figure it out.

351
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,800
<i>But you can't mentor me forever.</i>

352
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:43,440
So this time, I want to try
handling it all on my own.

353
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:46,520
- Think your wings are fully grown?
- <i>No.</i>

354
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:49,520
I almost had my feathers plucked
a few days ago.

355
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:52,680
It was just so embarrassing.
I didn't want you to see.

356
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:54,240
So humiliating.

357
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:55,320
How humiliating?

358
00:21:57,280 --> 00:22:00,880
Humiliating enough that I cried
in front of someone.

359
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:09,480
<i>But experience comes from lessons learned.</i>

360
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:12,680
The hurdles I'm facing now
will become my greatest assets.

361
00:22:12,760 --> 00:22:14,520
Once I get over this mountain,

362
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:16,360
I'll be unstoppable. Right?

363
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,000
You're pretty confident.

364
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:22,320
Guess I was worrying for nothing.

365
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:25,160
<i>Just in case… I mean, just in case.</i>

366
00:22:25,240 --> 00:22:28,400
If you ever need help, come to me anytime.

367
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,360
Forget it.

368
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:33,160
I don't want to be a third wheel
between you and all those women.

369
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:37,000
XIAOXI

370
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,080
<i>Hello, Xinzhi.</i>

371
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:43,360
Ms. Liu, hold on a second. I have…

372
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:44,360
I'm off.

373
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:50,800
Is that why you haven't been
contacting me lately?

374
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:09,040
Ye Xinzhi, do you really…

375
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:15,680
not have that kind of feelings for me?

376
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:30,040
What did you just say? Bad signal.

377
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:34,240
Nothing.

378
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:39,560
I just meant, uh,

379
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:42,080
if you keep ruining people's plans,
karma will come for you.

380
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:46,520
I wouldn't want that
to mess up my own love life.

381
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:50,360
<i>And lately, I've been handling</i>
<i>basic business</i>

382
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:52,280
with Celestial's salespeople.

383
00:23:52,360 --> 00:23:54,280
If you have new work for me,

384
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:55,960
I probably won't be able to do it.

385
00:23:57,280 --> 00:24:00,120
Okay. I'll be away on business
for a few days.

386
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:02,560
So I'll give you some time off. Good luck.

387
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,240
You too.

388
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:16,360
Love life?

389
00:24:24,840 --> 00:24:26,440
Can't keep going like this.

390
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:31,520
Absolutely cannot.

391
00:24:39,120 --> 00:24:40,000
CELESTIAL INSURANCE CONSULTING PROPOSAL
INTERNAL SELECTION

392
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:40,920
BU TIANNA: 4 VOTES

393
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:42,360
Zhou Sen got one vote.

394
00:24:43,360 --> 00:24:44,480
Yang Rui got two votes.

395
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:46,840
Bu Tianna got…

396
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:51,840
four votes.

397
00:24:51,920 --> 00:24:53,520
Alright. Let's hear it.

398
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:55,400
Why did you all choose
Bu Tianna's proposal?

399
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:58,040
Her data is very detailed.

400
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:01,440
The overall internet transformation budget
is reduced by 30%.

401
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:03,480
One reason Celestial
rejected the previous proposal

402
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,120
was that the budget was too high.

403
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:07,640
I think this one will definitely work.

404
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:10,600
Okay. Since it's the group's choice,

405
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:12,440
let's have Tianna present!

406
00:25:16,880 --> 00:25:18,400
INTELLIGENT UNDERWRITING & CLAIMS
MVP SOLUTION

407
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:31,280
Not bad.

408
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:34,440
- Mr. Zheng.
- Mr. Zheng. We still--

409
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:39,600
Now, I'd like to present Plan B
to everyone.

410
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,200
Xu Chi, you--

411
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:00,080
You…

412
00:26:00,840 --> 00:26:02,520
Speak up a little, okay?

413
00:26:03,120 --> 00:26:04,040
The people in the back can't hear you.

414
00:26:04,120 --> 00:26:06,400
A good proposal
needs to be heard by everyone.

415
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:07,600
Okay.

416
00:26:08,760 --> 00:26:11,160
Today, I'm only going to speak plainly.

417
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:14,360
If we went with last month's old proposal,

418
00:26:14,440 --> 00:26:17,760
Celestial's annual premium growth
could hit 20%,

419
00:26:17,840 --> 00:26:20,600
but it would also cut commissions in half

420
00:26:20,680 --> 00:26:25,040
for agents and salespeople
with below-median KPIs.

421
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:26,560
But this proposal aims

422
00:26:26,640 --> 00:26:30,120
to boost Celestial's
annual premium growth to 30%,

423
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:32,360
while also increasing

424
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:34,880
salespeople's income by 10% annually.

425
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:38,360
You probably think
I'm selling you a pipe dream, right?

426
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:40,760
Because I know that to many people,

427
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:42,640
consultants are just smooth talkers.

428
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:46,720
But I'm pretty confident in my proposal,

429
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:49,280
so give me half an hour.

430
00:26:49,360 --> 00:26:51,040
Hear me out
before you decide to tear into me.

431
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,640
Okay. Let's get started.

432
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:59,120
To be fair,
our previous versions weren't bad.

433
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:01,400
So why, after so many iterations,

434
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:03,560
has Celestial's acceptance remained low?

435
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:06,400
We've actually been thinking it over
and reflecting on it since we got back.

436
00:27:06,480 --> 00:27:09,520
After the whole team's
on-the-ground research,

437
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:11,240
we finally figured out the problem.

438
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:14,200
If Celestial actually
accepted our proposal,

439
00:27:14,280 --> 00:27:17,520
it would mean opening up
all your business data to Maxmise.

440
00:27:17,600 --> 00:27:19,880
That would certainly be
a big win for Maxmise,

441
00:27:19,960 --> 00:27:23,720
but for Celestial, there's real risk.

442
00:27:23,800 --> 00:27:27,440
That has been a hidden concern
for your senior leadership.

443
00:27:27,520 --> 00:27:29,440
And for the sales side,

444
00:27:29,520 --> 00:27:32,640
everyone's worried about things like,
once they go digital,

445
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:33,880
how much departmental profit

446
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:35,480
would get taken
by the Internet Business Division,

447
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:37,800
and whether they'd be able
to keep their own clients.

448
00:27:37,880 --> 00:27:38,720
Don't worry, everyone.

449
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:42,160
Because what we're doing for Celestial
this time isn't about subtraction.

450
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:43,160
It's about addition.

451
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:12,240
In short, the new app,

452
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:14,120
the digital marketing content center,

453
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:17,040
and the Agent Cooperation Network
being built on the middle platform

454
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:18,760
are all traffic and efficiency tools

455
00:28:18,840 --> 00:28:21,320
that frontline salespeople
can actually use.

456
00:28:21,920 --> 00:28:22,960
Let me wrap this up in a nutshell.

457
00:28:23,040 --> 00:28:25,160
The digital transformation this time

458
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:26,800
isn't about making things
harder for everyone.

459
00:28:26,880 --> 00:28:29,480
It's about helping you close deals
and make money.

460
00:28:46,920 --> 00:28:49,240
THANK YOU FOR LISTENING

461
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:51,400
Now that's the right approach.

462
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:53,880
The earlier proposals
were like listening to Greek.

463
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:03,600
Mr. Pi, today's proposal was excellent.

464
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:05,680
We'll go back and study it carefully

465
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:07,440
- and get back to you soon.
- Alright.

466
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:09,360
Especially Miss Xu.

467
00:29:09,440 --> 00:29:11,760
Her proposal was very solid.

468
00:29:11,840 --> 00:29:13,040
You flatter me.

469
00:29:13,120 --> 00:29:15,880
This proposal reflects the consensus
of the entire project team.

470
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:18,000
I was just the presenter.

471
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:20,320
But you're the one who spent

472
00:29:20,400 --> 00:29:22,080
over two weeks working alongside
our salespeople.

473
00:29:22,760 --> 00:29:24,880
- Mr. Zheng, I have to be honest with you.
- Oh?

474
00:29:24,960 --> 00:29:27,760
Consulting firms have worked
with Celestial quite a bit,

475
00:29:27,840 --> 00:29:31,360
but Miss Xu is the most hands-on person
I've ever seen.

476
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:32,960
- Exactly.
- Most importantly,

477
00:29:33,040 --> 00:29:34,040
Miss Xu speaks in plain language.

478
00:29:34,120 --> 00:29:36,440
Everyone can understand what she says.

479
00:29:36,520 --> 00:29:38,000
I'm just a translator.

480
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:39,440
I took Mr. Pi and Ma Ke's ideas

481
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:40,760
and put them in simple terms.

482
00:29:40,840 --> 00:29:42,520
Everyone helped me a lot.

483
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:45,400
Xu Chi, look at all this praise.

484
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:46,640
I need to remind you of something.

485
00:29:46,720 --> 00:29:48,360
This is just the first step
of a long journey.

486
00:29:48,440 --> 00:29:50,880
A project this big
requires careful attention. Okay?

487
00:29:50,960 --> 00:29:51,880
Can't afford any mistakes.

488
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:53,480
If something goes wrong… Right?

489
00:29:53,560 --> 00:29:56,360
- Mr. Pi, the follow-up--
- Ma Ke has a point.

490
00:29:56,440 --> 00:29:58,200
If anything goes wrong…

491
00:30:01,840 --> 00:30:02,920
deduct his pay.

492
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:04,800
Mr. Zheng, after you.

493
00:30:14,440 --> 00:30:15,640
Thank you for giving me the opportunity.

494
00:30:16,840 --> 00:30:18,280
You earned the opportunity yourself.

495
00:30:19,280 --> 00:30:20,200
No need to thank me.

496
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:23,800
The slides you praised Ma Ke for that day

497
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:26,800
were almost identical
to what I'd shown him the night before.

498
00:30:26,880 --> 00:30:29,080
And after he saw my presentation,

499
00:30:29,160 --> 00:30:31,960
he assigned me to work
on a completely new, unfamiliar proposal.

500
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:35,240
That's why I performed so poorly
at the meeting that day.

501
00:30:37,040 --> 00:30:38,640
I pretended I couldn't find something.

502
00:30:39,520 --> 00:30:40,600
Where is it?

503
00:30:41,400 --> 00:30:42,760
I left it right on the desk.

504
00:30:42,840 --> 00:30:44,760
Zhao Heng, have you seen my USB drive?

505
00:30:44,840 --> 00:30:46,560
USB drive? What color?

506
00:30:47,160 --> 00:30:49,080
The yellow one.

507
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:50,840
I remember putting it in that box.

508
00:30:50,920 --> 00:30:52,400
How is it not there?

509
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:57,000
Found it?

510
00:30:57,080 --> 00:30:59,640
<i>Just a girl who panics</i>
<i>over a little criticism.</i>

511
00:30:59,720 --> 00:31:02,320
<i>I was worried she might push back</i>
<i>after being set up,</i>

512
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:04,200
<i>but she's even more timid than I thought.</i>

513
00:31:04,280 --> 00:31:05,160
MA KE

514
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:07,200
I asked Security for the footage

515
00:31:07,280 --> 00:31:09,840
and gathered the evidence
while Ma Ke wasn't on guard.

516
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:13,160
But Mr. Pi, I'm not here to complain.

517
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:17,120
I'm here to fight for a chance.

518
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:22,080
This is the first draft of a new proposal
I developed independently.

519
00:31:22,160 --> 00:31:23,280
Please take a look.

520
00:31:23,360 --> 00:31:24,240
If you think it's good,

521
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:25,960
I'd like to skip
the internal review competition

522
00:31:26,040 --> 00:31:27,400
and present directly to Celestial.

523
00:31:27,480 --> 00:31:29,560
If Celestial rejects it, I'll resign.

524
00:31:38,560 --> 00:31:39,400
Xu Chi,

525
00:31:40,560 --> 00:31:42,960
have you thought
about what happens if you fail?

526
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:45,440
You're gambling with your career.

527
00:31:45,520 --> 00:31:46,760
I'm not gambling.

528
00:31:46,840 --> 00:31:49,240
I'm taking control of my own destiny.

529
00:31:50,280 --> 00:31:53,960
You awarded me the YangFan Cup
championship trophy.

530
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:56,640
So you know my talent and capabilities
better than anyone.

531
00:31:58,200 --> 00:32:00,000
Ms. Sha was promoted by you.

532
00:32:00,080 --> 00:32:03,160
She says she loves
ambitious, capable subordinates.

533
00:32:04,120 --> 00:32:05,120
I believe you do too.

534
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:15,240
Congratulations. You won your gamble.

535
00:32:15,320 --> 00:32:18,600
And your presentation
was even better than the slides I saw.

536
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:23,160
We used to take a disruptive approach,

537
00:32:23,240 --> 00:32:24,640
constantly challenging
our clients' existing systems.

538
00:32:24,720 --> 00:32:29,440
But most people push back
when you try to overturn everything.

539
00:32:30,960 --> 00:32:34,960
They prefer validation and consensus
from consultants.

540
00:32:35,040 --> 00:32:36,480
And what they really want is…

541
00:32:38,800 --> 00:32:40,560
What they really want is a solution

542
00:32:40,640 --> 00:32:42,760
- that truly addresses their anxieties.
- Exactly.

543
00:32:44,360 --> 00:32:47,640
If the project moves forward smoothly,
Maxmise as a whole

544
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:49,760
benefits the most.

545
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:53,640
But it's just a normal progression,

546
00:32:53,720 --> 00:32:56,440
so there won't be any bonus for you,

547
00:32:56,520 --> 00:32:59,000
and Ma Ke won't be penalized either.

548
00:33:01,600 --> 00:33:02,440
I understand.

549
00:33:03,120 --> 00:33:04,960
Company management is complicated.

550
00:33:05,040 --> 00:33:06,440
Too clean a system
leaves no room for flexibility.

551
00:33:06,520 --> 00:33:07,800
And I just emphasized

552
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:10,520
that the credit belongs to Ma Ke
and the entire project team.

553
00:33:12,200 --> 00:33:14,400
Ma Ke is actually a smart guy.

554
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:15,840
You helped him save face.

555
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:17,080
He'll return the favor.

556
00:33:18,520 --> 00:33:19,360
You know what?

557
00:33:20,640 --> 00:33:22,280
You're bolder than anyone else.

558
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:26,360
And you have a clearer vision
for the future.

559
00:33:26,440 --> 00:33:27,400
So from now on,

560
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:29,440
I'll hold you to a higher standard.

561
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:32,080
What standard?

562
00:33:32,840 --> 00:33:36,320
Does that mean I can't use GPS
to count sheep anymore?

563
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:37,360
Switch to BeiDou?

564
00:33:38,760 --> 00:33:40,080
You know that joke too.

565
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:44,240
Humor is actually a great weapon.

566
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:47,400
Remember to use it more often.

567
00:33:56,760 --> 00:33:59,200
- Xu Chi. Congratulations.
- Thanks.

568
00:33:59,800 --> 00:34:00,720
Well done, Xu Chi.

569
00:34:08,600 --> 00:34:09,760
Ma, you're back.

570
00:34:09,840 --> 00:34:11,400
Spare me the chatter. Get back to work.

571
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:20,520
Chi.

572
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:23,719
You're back. No. Sit down. Sit.

573
00:34:25,360 --> 00:34:27,639
Uh, let me talk to you.

574
00:34:34,360 --> 00:34:36,040
Well, come to my office.

575
00:34:38,400 --> 00:34:40,480
And, uh, no need to bring your laptop.

576
00:34:40,560 --> 00:34:41,800
Just got back. Pretty tired.

577
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:42,880
Put the laptop down.

578
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:55,760
She really stole the show this time.

579
00:34:55,840 --> 00:34:57,600
She came back in Mr. Pi's car.

580
00:34:58,760 --> 00:35:00,120
I heard Tianna had just finished

581
00:35:00,200 --> 00:35:02,120
when Xu Chi went straight up
and started presenting.

582
00:35:02,200 --> 00:35:03,160
Everyone was stunned.

583
00:35:03,240 --> 00:35:05,640
But it worked really well.
Absolutely crushed it.

584
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:08,560
Zhao Heng.

585
00:35:09,200 --> 00:35:10,280
What about your princess?

586
00:35:10,360 --> 00:35:11,400
Aren't you going to check on her?

587
00:35:12,560 --> 00:35:14,440
A princess doesn't need comforting.

588
00:35:14,520 --> 00:35:17,760
Not like us, weak commoners.

589
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:30,320
What a coincidence.

590
00:35:32,320 --> 00:35:33,160
Congratulations.

591
00:35:34,960 --> 00:35:35,840
Thanks.

592
00:35:37,640 --> 00:35:40,240
When I was watching you down there,
I was actually pretty scared.

593
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:41,800
Scared of what?

594
00:35:42,480 --> 00:35:43,920
Scared that if you get too good,

595
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:45,840
you won't have dinner with me anymore.

596
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:49,680
LET'S GO GET A GOOD MEAL LATER

597
00:35:56,480 --> 00:35:57,800
Depends on what we're eating.

598
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:06,120
You came back this afternoon, right?

599
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:07,800
Yeah.

600
00:36:07,880 --> 00:36:10,040
Tianhe is now with the project manager.

601
00:36:10,120 --> 00:36:11,160
From today on,

602
00:36:11,240 --> 00:36:13,880
I'm focusing on setting up
the game with Wen Ruosen.

603
00:36:14,480 --> 00:36:16,280
Wen Ruosen screwed you over

604
00:36:16,360 --> 00:36:20,120
almost ten years ago, right?

605
00:36:20,200 --> 00:36:22,800
I bet he never imagined
you'd still be holding onto this.

606
00:36:27,760 --> 00:36:28,720
Eat.

607
00:36:29,320 --> 00:36:31,240
Why are you on your phone
while eating too?

608
00:36:31,320 --> 00:36:32,520
Put it down.

609
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:34,320
Xu Chi sent me a file.
I need to take a look.

610
00:36:36,240 --> 00:36:37,320
What did the girl send you?

611
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:41,040
Pretty interesting.

612
00:36:42,320 --> 00:36:43,240
A few days ago,

613
00:36:43,320 --> 00:36:44,880
she ran into some issues on her project.

614
00:36:44,960 --> 00:36:46,400
I was going to help out,

615
00:36:46,480 --> 00:36:48,800
but she said
she wanted to handle it on her own.

616
00:36:48,880 --> 00:36:50,080
She didn't tell me the details.

617
00:36:50,680 --> 00:36:51,680
I was worried.

618
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:54,120
Then she just told me
she'd resolved it perfectly.

619
00:36:54,200 --> 00:36:55,640
And she sent me the project summary.

620
00:36:56,520 --> 00:36:58,080
She can write project summaries now?

621
00:36:58,160 --> 00:36:59,000
3-STEP STRATEGY

622
00:36:59,080 --> 00:37:00,640
Not bad at all. Wow.

623
00:37:02,600 --> 00:37:05,080
Bold, smart, and measured.

624
00:37:05,160 --> 00:37:06,480
The younger generation is formidable.

625
00:37:06,560 --> 00:37:07,960
Come on. Cheers.

626
00:37:08,040 --> 00:37:09,640
Let's celebrate. That's a good one.

627
00:37:09,720 --> 00:37:12,360
You've basically raised a thoroughbred.

628
00:37:13,240 --> 00:37:14,640
I'm telling you,

629
00:37:15,520 --> 00:37:17,120
once you retire,
you should just teach EMBA

630
00:37:17,200 --> 00:37:18,160
at a business school.

631
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:20,120
Teaching isn't my thing.

632
00:37:20,200 --> 00:37:21,080
In all these years,

633
00:37:21,680 --> 00:37:22,720
I've only come across one person like her.

634
00:37:24,600 --> 00:37:27,240
Wipe that look off your face. That…

635
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:29,280
That satisfied look. Get rid of it.

636
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:31,000
It's disgusting.

637
00:37:31,720 --> 00:37:33,880
Now I get why you like her.

638
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:36,720
Both of you got burned

639
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:38,720
and betrayed by your bosses.

640
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:40,400
Neither of you could swallow it,

641
00:37:40,480 --> 00:37:42,400
so you went straight for revenge.

642
00:37:42,480 --> 00:37:43,760
She succeeded.

643
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:46,600
- But I haven't.
- You admitted it.

644
00:37:48,240 --> 00:37:49,080
Admitted what?

645
00:37:49,160 --> 00:37:51,440
Admitted what? You admitted you like her.

646
00:37:51,520 --> 00:37:53,400
I just threw out a guess,
and I got it out of you.

647
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:55,240
You let your true feelings slip,
didn't you?

648
00:37:58,840 --> 00:37:59,680
Drink up.

649
00:38:00,720 --> 00:38:02,680
Changing the subject.
That just proves you admitted it.

650
00:38:02,760 --> 00:38:04,400
Just drink.

651
00:38:07,280 --> 00:38:09,920
Hey, what are you really thinking?

652
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:12,800
You clearly fell for her,

653
00:38:12,880 --> 00:38:15,600
but you haven't realized it
or figured it out.

654
00:38:15,680 --> 00:38:19,320
Do I have to knock some sense into you?

655
00:38:27,400 --> 00:38:29,320
Hey, you… Sit down. Listen to me.

656
00:38:29,400 --> 00:38:31,160
Let me ask you.

657
00:38:31,240 --> 00:38:33,520
When are you going to make it clear?

658
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:36,440
Look at me.

659
00:38:37,800 --> 00:38:40,440
I know you don't want to hear this,
but I have to say it.

660
00:39:12,120 --> 00:39:14,840
<i>You clearly fell for her,</i>

661
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:16,200
<i>but you haven't realized it</i>

662
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:17,880
<i>or figured it out, right?</i>

663
00:39:17,960 --> 00:39:19,720
<i>Do I have to knock some sense into you?</i>

664
00:39:33,040 --> 00:39:36,000
- Thanks. Drive safe.
- Good night.

665
00:39:50,280 --> 00:39:54,560
UNDERGROUND PARKING ENTRANCE

666
00:39:56,400 --> 00:39:58,640
- What a coincidence.
- Yeah.

667
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:00,360
What a coincidence.

668
00:40:09,400 --> 00:40:12,000
- He is…?
- My colleague.

669
00:40:12,080 --> 00:40:13,680
We're on the same project team.

670
00:40:15,440 --> 00:40:17,520
No wonder your Celestial project
went so smoothly.

671
00:40:17,600 --> 00:40:19,160
So it's the power of love.

672
00:40:20,360 --> 00:40:21,880
What are you talking about?

673
00:40:21,960 --> 00:40:23,360
We were just having a meal.

674
00:40:23,440 --> 00:40:26,560
At most, it's a date.

675
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:27,680
No need to be shy.

676
00:40:27,760 --> 00:40:32,320
I also find ways
to unwind in my spare time.

677
00:40:36,760 --> 00:40:38,280
Right.

678
00:40:38,360 --> 00:40:42,000
Exactly. I remember you told me
that to be a good consultant,

679
00:40:42,080 --> 00:40:44,480
you need to find an outlet
for your emotions.

680
00:40:44,560 --> 00:40:46,480
So I learned fast.

681
00:40:49,160 --> 00:40:50,280
Good student.

682
00:40:55,960 --> 00:40:58,560
I still have a lot to learn from you.

683
00:40:59,200 --> 00:41:01,200
Like how to…

684
00:41:11,680 --> 00:41:14,080
A prize from the beer I just got. For you.

685
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:19,400
I have a meeting.

686
00:41:19,480 --> 00:41:21,520
I'm heading off. Bye.
